Description: Keep the current directory and file across a terminal reset.
 A reset (RIS, DECSTR, DECSR, or vte_terminal_reset) clears every termprop, and since the current
 directory and file became termprops, set by OSC 7 and OSC 6, it clears those too. The shell does
 not learn about the reset and reports its directory again only at its next prompt. Until then a
 terminal application finds no directory, so a new tab or window opens in the home directory
 rather than where the shell is.
 .
 Both are kept, as they were before they became termprops. Every other termprop is still reset.
 .
 The selection lives in TrackingStore::reset_all_except so that it can be unit tested without a
 terminal. The test is added by keep-directory-on-reset-tests.patch.
